From: theycallmeboxy <82409831+theycallmeboxy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 08:07:55 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] panvk: allocate the gpu_prerast arenas on first use

The gpu_prerast arenas (64 MiB, plus 96 MiB for tessellation) were
allocated and fully committed when a device enabled geometry shaders,
tessellation, transform feedback, non-solid fill, viewport index output or
vertex-stage stores. DXVK enables those on every device, as D3D11 requires
them, so every DXVK game paid 160 MiB of GPU memory per VkDevice whether or
not it ever drew through gpu_prerast (most never do). The arenas are still
fully committed (growing them on GPU faults loses the first gpu_prerast
draw's output on MediaTek kbase), but now on the first draw that needs one,
under a device lock; if that allocation fails the command buffer fails with
VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_DEVICE_MEMORY.

Whether a device may use gpu_prerast is now kept in gpu_prerast_enabled /
gpu_prerast_tess_enabled, set from the features at creation as before, and
that, not whether the memory exists yet, decides the extra barrier
dependency on the compute subqueue, so barriers behave as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QAYrqSPd4TgpVaKLqz5cYR

Purpose: stop committing the gpu_prerast arenas (64 MiB + 96 MiB for tessellation) at device creation; DXVK enables the features that trigger them on every device, so every DXVK game paid up to 160 MiB per VkDevice; they are now allocated (still fully committed) on the first draw that needs them, and barrier behaviour keys on the enabled features as before
Upstream-commit: none (zenithblue fork code; the fork's own comment names lazy commit as the upgrade path)
Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC6 (Anbernic RG477M, Dimensity 8300, v11)
Tested Kbase UAPI: CSF 1.21 / MediaTek
Dependencies: none of ours; applies on the full g615-v11-csf series
Validation test: PanProbe 38/38 (geometry, tessellation, xfb, gs_viewport_depth, gs_tess_primitive_id pass); drawbench 8/8, racetest and msrtss identical; peak GPU memory Megabonk 1258 -> 1180 MB, Moonlighter 793 -> 637 MB, Valheim 2054 -> 1990 MB, same fps
Generated-by: LLM
